{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "An Emotional Week"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Why so Cranky?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 4}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Relate information about common solutions to problems."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.  "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.  "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.  "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.  "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.  "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.  "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.  "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.  "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le04ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking Hypothetically About the Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>, <span class=\"italic\">should have</span> and <span class=\"italic\">would have</span> to talk about things that were possible in the past and may or may not have happened. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure: <br/><br/> <span class=\"strong\">Subject    + modal verb    + have     + verb (past participle)</span><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I             could              have        done<br/> You             should              have        made<br/> She            would               have        said</span><br/><br/>  You use <span class=\"italic\">could have</span> to talk about possibilities if something had been different in the past.<br/> For example: <span class=\"italic\">It could have been avoided.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">should have</span> to talk about past events that did not happen and to speculate about events that may or may not have happened.<br/> For example: <span class=\"italic\">I should have taken my own advice."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">should not have</span> to speculate negatively about what may or may not have happened.<br/> You also use <span class=\"italic\">should not have</span> to express regret for past actions.<br/><br/>  You use <span class=\"italic\">would have</span> to imagine a result if something had been different in the past.<br/> For example: <span class=\"italic\">That would have been helpful. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "* <span class=\"italic\">Would have</span> expresses more certainty about the result than <span class=\"italic\">could have</span>."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I should have taken my own advice about being more aware of other people's emotions."}, {"type": "example", "content": "It could have been avoided. "}, {"type": "example", "content": " I should have written it down but I was busy and frazzled so I didn't. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "She should have written it down."}, {"type": "example", "content": "That would have been helpful."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Reported Speech and Questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use reported speech when you are saying (reporting) what other people said. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you tell people what someone has said in the past, you generally make the verb tense 'more in the past'. You need to change the verb to the next past form. <br/><br/>For example:<br/><br/>"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Direct Speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Reported Speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">like</span> him.\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">liked</span> him.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"I'<span class=\\\"strong\\\">m coming</span> to the party.\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">was coming.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"I already <span class=\\\"strong\\\">ate</span>.\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He said he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">had</span> already <span class=\\\"strong\\\">eaten</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">can</span> cook.\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He told me he <span class=\\\"strong\\\">could</span> cook.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"Where do you <span class=\\\"strong\\\">live</span>?\\\"\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He asked me where I <span class=\\\"strong\\\">lived</span>.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You have to change the pronoun if you are reporting what someone else said. Compare these two sentences. In each case the person actually said \"I don't want to go.\""}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>I said, \u201cI don't want to go.\u201d  >  I said <span class=\"strong\">I</span> didn't want to go.</li> <li>Bill said, \u201cI don't want to go.\u201d  >  Bill said <span class=\"strong\">he</span> didn't want to go.</li></ul>Look at the chart below to see the changes in verb tense."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":10,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Direct Speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Reported Speech\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Perfect\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Perfect Progressive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Future Simple (will)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Conditional (would)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal <span class=\\\"italic\\\">can</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal <span class=\\\"italic\\\">could</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal <span class=\\\"italic\\\">may\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal <span class=\\\"italic\\\">might\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal <span class=\\\"italic\\\">will\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Modal <span class=\\\"italic\\\">would\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "One of the waitresses told me a few days ago that she couldn't work yesterday."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I asked her why she wasn't at work. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "She reminded me that she had told me she couldn't work the shift. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "She told me that she was at a funeral. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "a bit"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a small portion, degree, or amount"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I got into a bit of an argument with one of my employees. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about reactions and behavior in different situations."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "aware"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "knowing that something, such as a situation, exists"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's important to be aware of other people's emotions. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "furious"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very angry"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I was furious!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "frazzled "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very tired"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I should have written it down but I was busy and frazzled so I didn't."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to yell"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to say something very loudly to get someone's attention"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I immediately started yelling at her. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to flip out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to become very excited or angry"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I flipped out on my co-worker yesterday."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "funeral"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a ceremony held for a dead person"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I attended my grandfather's funeral last week. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob07aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "immersed"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "fully involved in something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I was so immersed in myself that I didn't notice how upset she was."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le04ob07aud08"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Imagine that you have made a big mistake because of a misunderstanding."}, 